g as he admits to be  moving on to a few more callbacks later  in this episode Rick knows that Spencer  has a guns because Spencer did the same  thing last season stealing from the  pantry when he assumed no one else would  notice looking out for himself remember  Rick Grimes has that investigative  police training which makes it really  easy to determine if someone is a  gutless dumbass also I love this  callback with Enid in those green  balloons now remember back in episode 7  of last season she and Glenn uses  balloons as a way to signal the others  and then shortly after that Glen said  this to her people you love they made  you who you are they're still part of  you so Enid is keeping these balloons as  a way to remember Glenn it's  small moment but it's a really sweet way  to show that she still thinks about him  and she still remembers what he taught  her okay moving on so last episode  seemed to imply that Darrell still had  some fight in him because he refused to  say negan's name so why now has Darrell  gone pretty much completely reek say  nothing refusing to take his motorcycle  back or stay announced Andrea who maybe  his blinking will tell us just turned in  Farben oh it's just gibberish  he's just blinking what a surprise Brie  although I think Darrell might be  playing a part here he knows that if he  can play by negan's rules for right now  he might gain enough trust to officially  join negan's gang and then work as a  kind of double agent for Rick and his  people which is kind of something that  happens with another character in the  comics falou soon to tell but we'll see  then as negan leaves he tells Rick this  messed up line which the censors are  surprisingly okay with I just slit my  dick down your throat and you thanked me  for now  that's another moment taken directly  from the comics and it connects to that  service theme that I brought up earlier  so this line along with the image of  Rick holding Lucille it all has this  gross sexual connotation to it like Rick  has spent this entire episode  servicing negan see not all  interpretations of the show or pious and  saintly some are super dirty and then  real quick check out this mis'able  detail when the Savior's fans drive over  these two Walker's the wheel goes over  one of their heads crushing it so why  did the show go to the trouble for this  effect  that's because negan and the show wanted  these two batted down walkers to mirror  the two of Rick's friends that went down  in the same way and then lying there  with their brain spread out on the  ground is a clear reference to the image  when negan left Rick back in the season  premiere this is kind of like negan's  way of saying never forgive it's also  interesting how Rick looks at the sign  outside these gates vengeance for the  plunderers now this could be read as  ironic since Rick and his people were  totally just plundered doing nothing to  defend themselves or you could read it  as foreshadowing promise like eventually  Rick and his people will have their  vengeance but let's talk about this  face-off between Rick and Spencer now we  know from the earlier scene that Spencer  blames Rick for his parents deaths but  Rick calling him weak  triggers this hero complex inside of him  Austin Nichols actually said that he's  been using Spencer's desire to be a  leader like his mother was as the major  inspiration for his character but check  out Rick's cold-blooded response you say  anything like that again to me I'll  break your jaw knock your teeth out  now I love this for a few reasons one  Rick shows us that he can still be a  tough don't with me badass when he needs  to be also when Rick forces Spencer to  respond by saying yes it shows how negan  suppressive threatening ruling style is  starting to affect Rick but here's my  favorite part of this line it's a call  back way back to season two when Rick  says almost the exact same thing to  Shane I wanted to break your jaw let you  choke on y